<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Cash not main factor in airport sale - Canberra.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Cash not main factor in airport sale - Canberra.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian acting Treasurer John Fahey said on Wednesday the government was not selling the country's major airports as a &quot;dash for cash&quot; with price as the main factor in choosing buyers.</p>
<p>&quot;The government is not motivated in moving to sell long term leases for their (airports') operation in a 'dash for cash', an exercise in simply selling these leases to the highest bidder,&quot; Fahey told a Sydney conference on airport privatisation.</p>
<p>Community service would also be a major consideration, he said in a copy of his speech released in Canberra.</p>
</text>
